# Test Project Package References

Do not duplicate production `<PackageReference>` entries in test projects.

## Rules

- Test projects get production dependencies through `<ProjectReference>` only.
- Allowed test-only packages: `LTs.TestUtils`, `xunit`, `xunit.runner.visualstudio`, `Moq`, `coverlet.collector`, `Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk`.
- Never add a package to a test project because the project under test already references it (for example `LTs.Utils`, `LTs.Json`, `Autofac`).
- If a test needs container or composition behavior, add or use a public API on the production project (for example `CompositionRoot.ResolveDefaultServices()`) instead of referencing the container package in the test project.

## Example

```xml
<!-- BAD: duplicates LTs.Utils from the production project -->
<PackageReference Include="LTs.Utils" Version="10.0.0-preview2" />
<ProjectReference Include="..\Prefix.Area\Prefix.Area.csproj" />

<!-- GOOD -->
<PackageReference Include="LTs.TestUtils" Version="10.0.0-preview2" />
<ProjectReference Include="..\Prefix.Area\Prefix.Area.csproj" />
```
